.NET Standard reference assembly
================================================================================

The "references" artifact of maven/unity-compat (codenameone-unity-compat,
classifier references) holds the assemblies the C# scripts of a Unity project
are compiled against. One of them, netstandard.dll, is the .NET Standard 2.1
reference assembly from the NuGet package NETStandard.Library.Ref 2.1.0
(https://www.nuget.org/packages/NETStandard.Library.Ref/2.1.0), redistributed
unmodified. It declares the API of the .NET base library and contains no
implementation; it is read by the C# compiler and the translator at build time
and is never part of an application.

The package's LICENSE.TXT and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.TXT are kept verbatim in
maven/unity-compat/third-party/NETStandard.Library.Ref and ship inside the
artifact under META-INF/licenses/NETStandard.Library.Ref.

